  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed L-shaped dormer, by virtue of its scale and siting, would be a visually overbearing addition that dominates the rear roof slope and lacks any sense of subservience to the host dwelling. This is considered harmful to the overall character and appearance of the property and the wider terrace row and is therefore contrary to the design objectives of Policy 53 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposal fails to provide adequate provision for on-site cycle storage facilities and therefore fails to promote sustainable methods of transport for future occupiers. This is contrary to the aims of Policies 20 and 61 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The host dwelling is unsuitable for conversion from class C3 to Sui Generis (large HMO) in that it would result in the loss of a family-sized unit of less than 124sqm. The principle of development is therefore unacceptable. It would be an unsustainable form of development that causes harm to the housing size and mix of the borough, which directly conflicts with Policy 15 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoBodyText&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;In the absence of a legal agreement, the proposal fails to provide the necessary financial contributions to secure adequate mitigation against the Epping Forest Special Area of Conservation and therefore fails to comply with Policy 81 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024) and the Supplementary Planning Document - Planning Obligations (2017).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;In the absence of a legal agreement to restrict current and future occupiers in obtaining on-street parking permits, the proposal constitutes unsustainable development in that it does not promote sustainable transport, which conflicts with the objectives of Policies 60 and 66 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
